  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 210 PM EST Monday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Chilly and dry conditions are expected tonight. A \ngradual warming trend is expected for the remainder of the week with \ndry conditions continuing.  \n\nAfternoon wx analysis continues to show a positively tilted upper \ntrough extending from the western Atlantic to the Deep South. \nSurface high pressure over the OH Valley continues to build toward \nthe area, with precipitation confined to the Gulf Coast/Florida in \nassociation with a shortwave at the base of the upper trough. Mostly \nclear skies prevail with temperatures in the mid 50s. The surface \nhigh will remain in control through the rest of the week as upper \nridging gradually builds over the area, and a closed low forms near \nthe eastern Gulf Coast. This will lead to mostly sunny skies and a \nslow warming trend throughout the week with highs rising into the \nlower 60s on Tuesday, mid 60s Wednesday, and upper 60s-near 70F on \nThu/Fri. Morning lows remain around freezing inland through Thursday \nwith light winds all week due to the high nearby. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Above average temperatures persist this weekend with \ndry conditions continuing on Saturday. There is a chance for rain on \nSunday, though confidence in rainfall is low (especially inland).\n\nThe upper ridge gradually breaks down by the end of the week, while \nthe Gulf Coast low slowly tracks NE over the weekend. Highs remain \nin the 60s as the northern stream remains displaced well to our \nN/NW. The low is progged to track offshore of the VA/NC coast on \nSunday. This will lead to an increase in clouds. Depending on the \ntrack and strength of the low, rain is possible (with the best \nchance near the coast). However, confidence in any rainfall is low \nas the deterministic models and ensembles have a wide range of \nsolutions. A slight majority of the ensemble members have little to \nno rain area-wide with the low well offshore. However, a minority of \nthe members have a decent amount of rainfall near the coast. \nUnfortunately, confidence in an appreciable wetting rain is \nextremely low west of I-95 at this time.",
